acceptance criteria to satisfy:
  - EACH Keith profile SHALL map to a stable Composio user identity and SHALL maintain bounded resumable sessions without exposing provider API keys to the model or browser.
  - CONNECTED accounts SHALL expose toolkit, account identity, auth configuration, granted scopes, connection state, last health, selection precedence, and revocation.
  - THE integration SHALL use session-based hosted MCP for portable tool access and SHALL restrict toolkits and tools rather than enabling the full catalog by default.
  - TOOL discovery SHALL remain within context and schema budgets and SHALL preserve exact account selection when several accounts exist for one toolkit.
  - KEITH SHALL apply its own risk, approval, audit, cancellation, timeout, and result-redaction policy before and after every Composio MCP call.
  - A real-account suite SHALL prove connect, resume, discover, read, approval-gated write, multiple-account selection, expiry recovery, revocation, deletion, and cross-profile isolation.

